hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1816","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out and asked the people for water, and prayed two rak’ahs, during which he recited aloud.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1817","Muhammad ibn Mansour informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When it rained, he would say: “O God, make it a beneficial rain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1818","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi, the judge of Basra, told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to: If he saw something emerging on one of the horizons of the sky, he would abandon his work, even if it was during prayer. If God reveals it, he praises God, and if it rains, he says: “Oh God, give us a beneficial excuse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1819","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Yazid, who is the son of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father Shurayh, that Aisha I told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If he saw a cloud approaching from one of the horizons, he would leave whatever was in it, even if it was in Prayer until he receives it, and says: “O God, we seek refuge in You from the evil with which we were sent.” And if it rains, he says: O God, a beneficial forbearance. O God, forsake. beneficial, even if God reveals it and does not rain, thank God for that.”"
"1820","Abdul Wahhab bin Al-Hakam Al-Warraq told us, he said: Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a cloud, meaning clouds, his face would color and change, and he would enter, exit, and approach. And he turned away and when it rained, it was hidden from him. Aisha said: So I mentioned to him some of what I had seen of him. He said: “And who knows? Perhaps it is as some people said.” Hud: And when they saw it spreading toward their valleys, they said, “This is our rain shower.” Rather, it is something you hastened about, a wind in which is a painful punishment."
"1821","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whenever he saw a silhouette, his face would change, and he would enter and exit, and he would come forward and turn away. When it rained, he would go. On his authority, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: “He did not believe that it would be as God said.” And when they saw him crossing in the direction of their valleys, they said this. A rainy season brings us to a wind in which there is a painful torment."
"1822","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Saleh bin Kaysan told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for us the morning prayer in Al-Hudaybiyyah, following the sky. It was during the night, so when he left, he went to the people and said: “Do you know what He said: Your Lord?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “ He said: One of My servants has become a believer and a disbeliever. As for whoever says: We have been given rain by the grace and mercy of God, that is a believer in Me and a disbeliever in the planet. As for whoever says: It rained on us under such-and-such a storm, he is a disbeliever in Me, a believer in the star.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1823","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled, he said: It rained on the people during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Did you not hear what your Lord said tonight?” He said: “What You have bestowed upon me.” My servants have no blessing except that a group of them become disbelievers therein, saying: We received rain under such-and-such storm, and under such-and-such storm. As for whoever believes in me, And whoever praises Me for giving me water, that is the one who believed in Me, but disbelieved in the star, and whoever says: We gave rain under such-and-such storm, that is the one who disbelieved in Me. And he believed in the star.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1824","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: I am Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubaid informed me Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your Lord said: What You have bestowed upon me My servants have not received any blessing except that a group of them became disbelievers in it, saying: “The star,” and “by the star.”"
"1825","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Attab bin Hunayn, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God had withheld rain from His servants for five years, and then sent it, it would have been A group of people who are disbelievers say: We were given water to drink the tawny of glory.”"
"1826","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: We were struck by rain, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out May God bless him and grant him peace. He was sad until the rain hit him, and he was told: Why did you do this? He said: “It is a hadith of a covenant with his Lord.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I did not understand what happened to us, nor was he saddened as you intended."
"1827","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The rain failed one year, so some Muslims rose to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a Friday, said: O Messenger of God, the rain has fallen, the land has become barren, and wealth has perished. He said: So he raised His hands, and we did not see a cloud in the sky, so he stretched out his hands until I saw the whites of his armpits asking God for rain. We had not prayed Friday until the young man nearby began to worry. The house is to return to its people. He said: It lasted a Friday, and when the next Friday came, they said: O Messenger of God! The houses were destroyed, and the riders were trapped. He said: Then he smiled at the quick boredom of the son of Adam, and said with his hand: “O God, help us, or be against us.” And it was dispersed from the city.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1828","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told me, he said: Abu Amr told me, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: A year befell the people during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon on the pulpit on the day Friday, then a Bedouin stood up and said: O Messenger of God, money has perished, and the children are hungry, so pray to God for us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised And he held out his hands, and we did not see a quiver in the sky, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, he did not put them down until clouds like mountains arose, then he did not descend from the sky. from his pulpit until I saw rain falling on his beard, so it rained on us that day, and the next day, and the next until the next Friday, so he stood up. That Bedouin, or someone else said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the building collapsed, and the money sank, so pray to God for us, and he raised The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his hands and said: “Oh God, be around us, or against us.” Then he did not point with his hand to a part of the cloud, but it opened until The city became like a deep hole, and the valley flowed, and no one came from any direction without speaking, meaning a good place."
"1829","I am Qutaybah bin Saeed. He said: It was narrated by Hammad, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed The sun and the moon are two signs of God. They are not eclipsed by anyone’s death or his life, but God frightens His servants through them.”"
"1830","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abu Masoud is Saeed bin Iyas. Al-Jariri, on the authority of Hayyan bin Umair, who said: Narrated by Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, who said: “While I was investing in my shares in the city, it collapsed.” The sun, so I gathered my arrows and said: Let us see what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had narrated regarding the solar eclipse. So I went to him from the time after his noon, and he was In the mosque, he started praising God, saying “Allahu Akbar,” and making supplications until he was unable to do so, then he got up and prayed two rak’ahs and four prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1831","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Then the sun was eclipsed, so he jumped up, dragging his garment, and prayed two rak’ahs until it became clear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1832","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Zaida told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, he said: I heard Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah, he says: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Abraham died, so the people said: It eclipsed because of Abraham's death. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sun and the moon are two of the signs of God. They are not eclipsed by the death of anyone or his life, so if You have seen it, so pray to God and pray until it is revealed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1833","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, that Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim told him, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse due to the death of anyone or his life. But they are a sign of God, so when you see them, pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1834","Ya'qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Qais told me, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are not eclipsed due to the death of anyone, but they are two signs of God, so when you see them, pray.”"
"1835","Muhammad bin Kamil Al-Marwazi told us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs of God, and they do not become eclipsed due to the death of anyone or his life. So when you see them, So pray until you are saved.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1836","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Khaled informed us, he said: Ash’ath reported to us, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: we were Sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Then the sun was eclipsed, so he jumped up, dragging his garment, and prayed two rak’ahs until it set.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1837","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, he said: Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a caller, and he called out, “Indeed, prayer is unified,” so they gathered together. They lined up, and he led them in four rak'ahs, with two rak'ahs and four prostrations.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1838","Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, he said: Bishr ibn Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sun eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out May God bless him and grant him peace, he went to the mosque, stood up, lined up the people behind him, and completed four rak’ahs and four prostrations, and the sun rose before it rose. \"He goes away\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1839","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Aliya, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Tawus, On the authority of Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed eight rak’ahs and four prostrations at the time of an eclipse,” and on the authority of Ata’ like that."
"1840","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed during a solar eclipse, so he recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited. Then he bowed, then he prostrated, and the other was like it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1841","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed told me, he said: Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Ibn Nimr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Kathir bin Abbas, and Amr told me Ibn Uthman, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Kathir Ibn Abbas informed me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abbas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “On the day of the solar eclipse, he prayed four rak’ahs in two rak’ahs, and four prostrations.”"
"1842","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Ubaid bin Umair speaking, he said Someone I believe told me, so I thought he meant Aisha, because she said: “The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he stood up.” He stood with the people intensely, then he bowed, then he stood, then he bowed, then he stood, then he bowed, then he bowed two rak’ahs, in each He prayed three rak'ahs, bowed the third, then prostrated, to such an extent that some men on that day will faint, and even pools of water will be poured on them from what He did it. He stood up when he bowed and said, “Allahu Akbar,” and when he raised his head, he said, “God hears those who praise Him.” He did not leave until the sun rose. So he stood up, thanked God, and praised Him, and said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse due to the death of anyone or his life, but two of the verses God will frighten you because of them, so when they are overshadowed, then rush to the remembrance of God until they are cleared.”"
"1843","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, regarding the verses of prayer, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He prayed ten rak’ahs in four prostrations.” I said to Mu’adh: On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him? He said: No doubt, no doubt (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1844","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Umayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The prayer of the verses is six rak’ahs with four prostrations.”"
"1845","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, both on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir said: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, son of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so the people said: The sun eclipsed only because of the death of Abraham, so he rose. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in six rak’ahs in four prostrations. He said takbeer, then he read, and he prolonged the recitation, then he bowed in the same way as he had stood, then he raised his head, and he recited without the first reading, then he bowed. In a manner similar to what he stood up, then he raised his head and recited without the second recitation, then he bowed in a manner similar to what he stood, then he raised his head and descended to prostrate. So he prostrated two prostrations, then he got up and performed three rak’ahs before prostrating. There is no rak’ah in it except that the one before it is longer than the one after it, except that his bowing is similar to his standing, then he delayed in his prayer. The rows continued with him, then he advanced and stood in his place, and the rows advanced, so he completed the prayer and the sun had risen, and he said: “O people! The sun and the moon are two of the signs of God Almighty, but they are not eclipsed by the death of a human being, so if you see any of that, pray until Deliver me, for there is nothing you are promised that I have not seen in this prayer of mine, and He has come with fire. That is when you saw me, I delayed for fear that I was afflicted by its brilliance, so much so that I said: Yes, Lord, while I was among them, and I saw the owner of the shop dragging his reed through the fire. He was robbing the pilgrim. With his socket, and if he was aware of it, he said: It was only attached to my socket, but if he neglected it, he took it away, and until I saw the owner of the cat in it. Which you bound, and did not feed it, and did not let it eat of the vermin of the land until it died of hunger, and Paradise was brought. That was when you saw me. I moved forward until I stood in my position, and I extended my hand, intending to take some of its fruit so that you could see it, but then it seemed to me that I would not do so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1846","Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The sun eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he stood up, said “Allahu Akbar,” and the people lined up behind him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited. He, peace and blessings be upon him, recited a long recitation, then he said “Allahu Akbar” and bowed for a long time, then he raised his head and said: “God hears those who praise Him. Our Lord, praise be to You.” Then he got up and recited a long recitation, which was shorter than the first recitation, then he said “Allahu Akbar”, and bowed for a long time, which was shorter than the first bowing, then he said “Allahu Akbar”. He said: “God hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, and praise be to You.” Then he prostrated, then he did the same in the other rak’ah, completing four rak’ahs. He performed four prostrations, and the sun set before he left. Then he got up and addressed the people, and praised God as he deserved, then he said: The sun and the moon are two signs of God, the Almighty, the Majestic. They are not diminished by the death or life of anyone, so when you see them, pray until they are released. “On your behalf,” and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In this position of mine I have seen everything, and you were promised, and then you saw me wanting to take When you saw me I moved forward, and I saw Hell destroying one another. When you saw me, I lagged behind, and I saw in it a son. “Lahiy, and it is He who leaves the impurities.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1847","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so a comprehensive prayer was called, and the people gathered and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in prayer.” Four rak'ahs in two rak'ahs and four prostrations.\""
"1848","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The sun eclipsed during the reign of The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led the people in prayer. Then he stood and prolonged his standing, then he bowed, and prolonged his bowing. Then he stood up and stood for a long time, which was shorter than the first standing. Then he bowed, and prolonged the bowing, which was shorter than the first bowing. Then he rose and prostrated. Then he did the same in the other rak’ah, then he left and the sun had risen, so he addressed the people, thanking God and praising Him, then he said: “ The sun and the moon are two signs of God. They do not eclipse due to anyone’s death or his life. So if you see that, then pray to God and say “Allahu Akbar.” And they gave in charity, then he said: O nation of Muhammad, there is no one more jealous than God if his servant commits adultery or his female slave commits adultery, O nation of Muhammad, and God, if \"You know what I know. You laughed little and wept a lot.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1849","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that Amra told him, that Aisha told her that a Jewish woman came to her and said: May God protect you from the torment of the grave. Then Aisha said: O Messenger of God! People will be tortured in graves? The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God forbid.” Aisha said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out and it collapsed. The sun rose, so we went out to the room, and the women gathered to us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us in the morning, and he stood for a long time. Then he bowed for a long time, then he raised his head, so he stood without standing the first time, then he bowed without bowing, then he prostrated, then he stood up the second time, so he did Like that, except that his bowing and standing were without the first rak’ah. Then he prostrated, and the sun appeared. When he left, he sat on the pulpit and said: He said: “People will be tried in their graves like the Antichrist.” Aisha said: And we used to hear him after that seeking refuge from the torment of the grave. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1850","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: I heard Umrah, she said: I heard Aisha, saying: A Jewish woman came to me asking me, and she said: May God protect you from the torment of the grave. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, I said: O Messenger God, will people be tortured in graves? He said: “God forbid,” so he boarded a boat, then mentioned a word that meant it, and the sun went down, so I was among the stones with women, so he came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got off his boat, came to his place of prayer, led the people in prayer, then he stood up, and prolonged his standing, then he bowed, and prolonged his bowing. Then he raised his head, so he prolonged his standing, then he bowed, so he prolonged his bowing, then he raised his head, so he prolonged his standing, then he prostrated, so he prolonged his bowing. He prostrated, then he stood up, and he stood up easier than his first standing, then he bowed, easier than his first bowing, then he raised his head, so he stood up easier than his first standing. The first, then he bowed easier than his first bowing, then he raised his head and stood easier than his first standing, so it was four rak’ahs and four prostrations. And the sun rose, and he said: “You will be tried in the graves like the trial of the Antichrist.” Aisha said: I heard him after that seeking refuge from the torment of The grave"
"1851","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim told me, he said: I am Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha: that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He prayed four rak’ahs and four prostrations during an eclipse in the row of Zamzam.”"
"1852","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Ali al-Hanafi told us, he said: Hisham, the companion of al-Dastawai, told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a very hot day, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed with his companions. So he prolonged standing until they made them fall down, then he bowed, and prolonged, then he raised, and prolonged, then he kneeled, and prolonged, then he raised, and prolonged, Then he prostrated two prostrations, then he got up, and he did something similar to that, and he began to move forward, then he began to fall behind, so it was four rak’ahs, and four prostrations, and he said: “They used to say: The sun and the moon do not eclipse except due to the death of a great one of their great ones, and that they are two signs of God. He will show you them, so when it sinks, pray until it sinks.”"
"1853","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: “The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he gave orders and the prayer was called.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer two rak’ahs and a prostration, then he stood up and prayed two rak’ahs and a prostration,” Aisha said: I have never kneeled so deeply, nor have I ever prostrated longer than him."
"1854","Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salam, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Katheer, on the authority of Abu Tu’ma, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: “The sun was eclipsed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kneeled and prostrated two times, then he got up and bowed.” He performed two rak'ahs and two prostrations, then he was removed from the sun.\" Aisha used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not prostrate, nor did he He kneeled longer than him"
"1855","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Zaid Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, He said: Abu Hafsa, Aisha’s servant, told me that Aisha told him: “When the sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, performed ablution and ordered that a call be made that the prayer should be completed, so he stood up and prolonged his prayer. Aisha said: “I thought he had recited Surat Al-Baqarah, then he bowed, and prolonged his bowing, then he said: “Allah hears those who praise Him.” Then he stood, just as he had stood, and did not prostrate, then he bowed, So he prostrated, then he got up and did the same as he had done, two rak’ahs and one prostration, then he sat down and turned away from the sun.”"
"1856","Hilal bin Bishr told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin al-Sa’ib, he said: Abu al-Sa’ib narrated to me, that Abd God Ibn Amr told him, he said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose to He prayed, and those with him stood up, so he stood up, and prolonged his standing, then he bowed, and prolonged his bowing, then he raised his head, and prostrated, and prolonged his prostration. Then he raised his head, and sat, and prolonged his sitting, then he prostrated, and prolonged his prostration, then he raised his head, and stood, and performed the second rak’ah. Just like what he did in the first rak’ah: standing, bowing, prostrating, and sitting. Then he started blowing his nose at the end of his prostration of the second rak’ah, and crying. And he says: “You did not promise me this, and I am among them. You did not promise me this, and I am among them, and we ask your forgiveness.” Then he raised his head, And the sun rose, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and addressed the people, praising God and praising Him, then he said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs.” Of the signs of God, so if you see the eclipse of one of them, then strive to remember God, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad. Indeed, Paradise has come close to me. Even if I had stretched out my hand, I would have taken a sip of its pickings, and the fire was brought close to me, until I started blowing it out of fear that it would overwhelm you, until I saw in it A donkey woman was being tortured over a cat she had tied up and would not let it eat from the vermin of the land. She neither fed it nor gave it drink. She died, and I saw her gnawing at her when she approached, and her buttocks gnawing when she turned, and I even saw in her the companion of two Sabbaths, a brother The Banu Ad-Dā'ad was thrusting a two-pronged stick into the fire, and I even saw there the owner of the stalls who used to rob pilgrims with his stalls, leaning on His chamberlain is in the Fire, saying: “He only stole the chamberlain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1857","Muhammad bin Ubad Allah bin Abdul-Azeem told me, he said: Ibrahim Sablan told me, he said: Abbad bin Abbad Al-Muhallabi, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he stood up to pray for the people. So he stood for a long time, then he bowed, then he prolonged the bowing, then he stood up, so he prolonged the standing, which was less than the first standing, then he bowed, so he prolonged the bowing. It is short of the first bowing, then he prostrated and prolonged prostration, then he rose, then he prostrated and prolonged prostration, and it is short of the first prostration, then He stood up, prayed two rak'ahs, and did the same in them, then he prostrated two prostrations, and did the same in them until he finished his prayer, then he said: Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs of God, and they do not eclipse due to the death of anyone or his life. So if you see that, then be terrified. remembrance of God, and to prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1858","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Al-Hussein bin Ayyash told me, he said: Zuhayr told me, he said: Al-Aswad bin Qais told me, he said: Tell me Tha'labah bin Abbad Al-Abdi, from the people of Basra, said that he witnessed a sermon one day by Samurah bin Jundub, so he mentioned a hadith in his sermon, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Samurah ibn Jundub said: “One day, I and a boy from the Ansar were throwing two objects for us in a timely manner. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until when the sun was within two or three spears in the eye of the observer from the horizon, it became black, and one of us said To its companion: Go with us to the mosque. By God, the matter of this sun will be narrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among his nation. It happened. He said: So we went to the mosque, and we met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he went out to the people. He said: So he went forward and prayed, and he stood up. Like the longest standing among us in prayer, we never hear a voice from him, then he bowed for us. Like the longest we have ever kneeled in prayer, we never hear him. A voice, then he prostrated like the longest one of us has ever prostrated in prayer. We do not hear a voice from him. Then he did that in the second rak’ah like that. He said: “ Then the appearance of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rak’ah, so he said the salutations, thanked God, praised Him, testified that there is no god but God, and testified That he is His servant and His Messenger.” Summary"
"1859","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of al-Nu’man bin Bashir, he said: The sun set during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he went out, dragging his garment in fear, until he came to the mosque, and he did not stop praying until It eclipsed, and when it eclipsed, he said: “Some people claim that the sun and the moon do not eclipse except due to the death of a great among the greats, and that is not the case. The sun, The moon does not eclipse due to the death of anyone or his life, but they are two signs of God, and when God appears to any of His creation, it humbles itself. “For him, so when you see that, pray like the last prayer you have prayed from among the written ones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1860","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Amr bin Asim told me, that his grandfather Ubaid Allah bin al-Wazi’ told him, he said: Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani told us, On the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Qubaysah ibn Mukhariq al-Hilali, he said: The sun was eclipsed, and we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time. In Medina, he went out in fear, dragging his garment, and prayed two rak'ahs that he had done so long, and his departure coincided with the setting of the sun, so he thanked God and praised upon him, then he said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God, and they do not eclipse due to the death of anyone or his life, so if you see That is something, so pray like the most recent written prayer you have prayed.”"
"1861","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh told us, and he is Ibn Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Qubaisah Al-Bajli, that the sun eclipsed, so the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs until it set, then he said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon do not They will be eclipsed by the death of someone, but they are created by His creation, and God creates in His creation whatever He wills, and when God is revealed for some of His creation, submit to Him, so whatever happens, pray until it is cleared, or God will cause something to happen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1862","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Good news, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the sun and the moon go down, pray like the last prayer you prayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1863","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed when the sun was eclipsed, just like our prayer. He bowed and prostrated.”"
"1864","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “One day he went out in a hurry to the mosque, and the sun had just set, so he prayed until it set, then he said:” The people of pre-Islamic times used to say that the sun and the moon do not eclipse except due to the death of a great among the great people of the earth, and that the sun and the moon do not They are eclipsed due to the death of someone or his life, but they are two of His creations. God causes whatever He wills to His creation, and whichever of them is eclipsed, so pray. Until it is cleared or God causes something to happen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1865","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the sun eclipsed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out, dragging his robe until he reached the mosque, and he jumped. The people came to him, so he led us in two rak'ahs of prayer, and when it was revealed, he said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God, through which God frightens His servants. And they do not sink because of anyone’s death or his life, so when you see that, pray until what is wrong with you is revealed.” And that is because a son of his It was called Abraham who died, and some people said about that."
"1866","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him: He prayed two rak’ahs like your prayer, and mentioned the solar eclipse."
"1867","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Zayd bin Aslam told me, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abd God Ibn Abbas, he said: The sun eclipsed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, and the people were with him, so he stood for a long time. He said: something like Surah Al-Baqarah, he said: Then he bowed for a long time, then he rose, and stood for a long time, which was less than the first standing, then he bowed for a long time, It is less than the first bowing, then he prostrated, then he rose and stood for a long time, and it is less than the first standing, then he bowed for a long time, and it is without The first bowing, then he rose, and stood for a long time, which was less than the first standing, then he bowed for a long time, which was less than the first bowing, then he prostrated, Then he departed, and the sun had risen, and he said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God. They do not eclipse due to the death of anyone or his life, so if “You see that, so remember God.” They said: O Messenger of God! We saw you eating something in this position of yours, then we saw you sitting down and saying: “I saw Paradise, or I was shown Paradise, and I ate a bunch of it. Had I taken it, you would have eaten from it for the rest of the world, and I saw Hell, and I have never seen a sight like today, and I have seen most of its people being women.” They said: Why, O Messenger of God? He said: “Because of their disbelief.” It was said: Do they disbelieve in God? He said: “They disbelieve in marriage, and they disbelieve in benevolence. If you were good to one of them all the time, and then she saw something from you, she said: I did not see from you.” \"absolutely good\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1868","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Walid, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Nimr told us, that he: He heard al-Zuhri narrating, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he prayed four rak’ahs in four prostrations, and recited it aloud whenever he raised He shook his head and said: “God hears those who praise Him. Our Lord, praise be to You.”"
"1869","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Sulayman bin Kathir told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The sun went down during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and said the takbir. The people said the takbeer with him, and he recited the recitation aloud.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1870","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Yazid, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he got up, said the takbir, recited a recitation, and recited it out loud.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1871","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Ibn Abbad, a man of the slave family. Al-Qays, on the authority of Samurah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed with them during a solar eclipse, and we could not hear his voice.”"
"1872","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Miswar Al-Zuhri told us, saying: We are Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. peace be upon him, so he prolonged his standing, then he bowed, so he prolonged his bowing, then he raised himself, so he prolonged. Shu’bah said: And I think he said: in prostration. Like that, he began to cry during his prostration, blow his nose, and say: “My Lord, you did not promise me this, and I ask your forgiveness. You did not promise me this, and I Among them, and when he prayed, he said: Paradise was offered to me, so much so that if I stretched out my hand, I took some of its picking, and Hell was offered to me, and I began to blow. For fear that its heat might overwhelm you, and I saw therein a thief of the two camels of the Messenger of God, and I saw therein a brother of Banu Da`ad who stole the pilgrims. He said to him: This is the work of the slaughterhouse, and I saw in it a tall, black woman, being tortured over a cat that she had tied up, and she did not feed it or give it water. And you did not let it eat of the vermin of the earth until it died, and the sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone, nor for his life, but they are two signs. Of the signs of God, so if one of them fails, or he says: one of them does something of that, then strive to the remembrance of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1873","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir informed us, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Nimr, that he asked al-Zuhri about the Sunnah of prayer The eclipse, and he said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The sun was eclipsed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered, A man called out: “The prayer is unified.” The people gathered, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in prayer. He said “Allahu Akbar,” then he recited a long recitation. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and bowed for a long time, like his standing or longer, then he raised his head and said: “Allah hears those who praise Him,” then he recited a recitation. It was long, shorter than the first recitation. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and bowed down for a long time, shorter than the first bowing. Then he raised his head and said: “God heard me.” “For the one who praises Him.” Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated for a long time, like his bowing or longer. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his head. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated, then he said “Allahu Akbar.” So he stood up and recited a long recitation, which was shorter than the first one, then he said “Allahu Akbar” and bowed down, which was shorter than the first bowing, then he raised his head and said: “ “Allah hears those who praise Him.” Then he recited a recitation that was smaller than the first recitation in the second standing, then he said “Allahu Akbar” and bowed, one bow less than the first bowing. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his head and said: “Allah hears whoever praises Him.” Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated lower than his first prostration, then he recited the tashahhud, then said the salutation. Then he stood among them, thanked God, and praised Him, then said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or because of his life, but they are signs.” Of the signs of God, whichever of them is overtaken by it, or by one of them, then rush to God with the remembrance of prayer.”"
"1874","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Musa bin Dawud told me, he said: Nafi bin Omar told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed during the eclipse, so he stood and stood for a long time, then he bowed, and he prolonged the bowing, then he rose. So he stood up and stood for a long time, then he bowed down, then he bowed down for a long time, then he rose up, then he prostrated, then he prolonged his prostration, then he rose up, then he prostrated, then he prolonged it. He prostrated, then he stood up, so he prolonged his standing, then he bowed, so he prolonged his bowing, then he rose, so he prolonged his standing, then he bowed, so he prolonged his bowing, then He rose, then he prostrated, then prostrated for a long time, then he raised, then prostrated, then prostrated for a long time, then he raised, then he left.”"
"1875","Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that Amra told him that Aisha said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and the sun went down, so we went out to the room, and women gathered around us. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us at dawn, and he stood for a long time, then bowed for a long time, then raised his head. So he stood without standing the first time, then he bowed without bowing, then he prostrated, then he stood the second time, so he did the same thing except that his bowing and standing He performed the first rak’ah, then he prostrated, and the sun rose. When he left, he sat on the pulpit and said, among other things, “Indeed, people will be tried in their graves.” “The temptation of the Antichrist,” summary (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1876","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It eclipsed. The sun during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he stood up, prayed, and stood for a very long time, then he bowed, and bowed for a very long time, then he rose Then he stood for a very long time, which was lower than the first standing, then he bowed, then he prolonged the bowing, which was lower than the first bowing, then he prostrated, then rose. He raised his head, so he prolonged his standing, which was shorter than the first standing, then he bowed, and prolonged his bowing, which was shorter than the first bowing, then he raised his head, and prolonged it. He stood up, which was less than the first standing, then he bowed, and prolonged the bowing, and it was less than the first bowing, then he prostrated, and finished his prayer, and he He was removed from the sun, and he addressed the people, thanking God and praising Him, then he said: “The sun and the moon are not eclipsed due to the death of anyone, nor do For his life, so if you see that, pray, give alms, and remember God.” And he said: “O nation of Muhammad, there is no one more jealous than God. Whether his servant commits adultery or his female slave commits adultery, O nation of Muhammad, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1877","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud Al-Hafari, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abbad, on the authority of Samura, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon when the sun was eclipsed, and he said: “As for what follows.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1878","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, told us: Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: We were with the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then the sun went down, so he got up to the mosque dragging his robe from the wheel, so the people got up to him, and he prayed two rak’ahs as You are praying, and when she finished, he addressed us and said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God. For the death of one of them, so if you see the eclipse of one of them, pray and supplicate until what is wrong with you is revealed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1879","Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi told us, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The sun eclipsed, So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, terrified, fearing that the Hour would come, so he stood until he came to the mosque, where he stood and prayed with the longest standing and bowing. And prostration that I saw him do during prayer once, then he said: “Indeed, these signs that God sends are not for the death of anyone, nor for his life, but God He sends it to frighten His servants with it, so if you see any of it, be alarmed at its remembrance, supplication to it, and seeking its forgiveness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1880","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Idris, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babih, on the authority of Ya’la bin Umayyah, who said: I said to Omar bin Al-Khattab: There is no sin on you if you shorten the prayer if you fear, and the people have believed. Then Omar said: I was amazed at what you were amazed at, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he said: “It is charity that God has bestowed upon you.” So accept his charity.”"
"1881","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Umayyah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Khalid, that he said to Abdullah Ibn Omar: We find the urban prayer and the fear prayer in the Qur’an, but we do not find the travel prayer In the Qur’an, Ibn Umar said to him: “My brother’s son, God has sent to us Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we do not know anything, so we are only doing as We saw Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, do this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1882","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hushaym, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He left Mecca for Medina, fearing nothing but the Lord of the Worlds, so he prayed two rak’ahs.”"
"1883","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, Makkani, Khalid, told us, he said: Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “We were walking with the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, between Mecca and Medina, we fear no one but God; we pray two rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1884","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, he said: I heard Habib bin Ubaid He narrated, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Ibn Al-Samit, who said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab praying two rak’ahs in Dhul-Hulaifa, so I asked him about that. He said: “I am only doing what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing.”"
"1885","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I went out with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He traveled from Medina to Mecca, and he did not stop shortening the prayer until he returned and performed it in prayer for ten days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1886","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us, he said, my father informed us, he said: Abu Hamza informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “I prayed two rak’ahs with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while traveling, and two rak’ahs with Abu Bakr. And with Omar two rak'ahs.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1887","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Ibn Habib, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, On the authority of Omar, he said: “The Friday prayer is two rak’ahs, the breaking of the fast is two rak’ahs, the sacrifice is two rak’ahs, and the journey is two rak’ahs, complete without shortening it according to the words of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1888","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahim told me, he said: Zaid told me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid Abi Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Hatra prayer was made obligatory on the tongue of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Four rak’ahs, the travel prayer is two rak’ahs, and the fear prayer is one rak’ah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1889","Yaqoub bin Mahan told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Malik told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Aidh, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “God made it obligatory to pray on the tongue of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, four rak’ahs in the city, two rak’ahs when traveling, and in fear \"a rak'ah\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1890","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, in his hadith, on the authority of Khalid ibn al-Harith, who said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, who said: I heard Musa saying: Ibn Salamah said: I said to Ibn Abbas: How can I pray in Mecca if I do not pray in congregation? He said: “Two rak’ahs of the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1891","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah, he said: Qatada, that Musa bin Salamah told them He asked Ibn Abbas, he said: I said: I miss praying in congregation while I am in Batha. What do you think I should pray? He said: “Two rak’ahs of the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1892","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Haritha bin Wahb Al-Khuza’i, he said: “I prayed with... The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs in Mina as long as the people did. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1893","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, and Amr bin Ali told us, he said : Yahya bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Harithah bin Wahb, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed with us.” “In Mina, most of the people and its people prayed two rak’ahs.”"
"1894","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sulaym, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, That he said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mina, with Abu Bakr, with Omar two rak’ahs, and with Uthman two rak’ahs, starting from \"his principality\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1895","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid told us, on the authority of al-Amash, he said: Ibrahim told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, And Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “I prayed two rak’ahs in Mina with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1896","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: I am Jesus, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: Othman prayed in Mina Four times, until this reached Abdullah, and he said: “I have prayed two rak’ahs with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1897","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He saluted two rak’ahs at Mina, two rak’ahs with Abu Bakr, and two rak’ahs with Omar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1898","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar told me, On the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs at Mina, Abu Bakr prayed two rak’ahs, and Omar prayed two rak’ahs. And Uthman prayed two rak’ahs of it early in his caliphate.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1899","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “We went out with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Medina to Mecca, and he led us in two rak’ahs of prayer until we returned. I said: Did he stay in Mecca? He said: “Yes, we performed it ten times.”"
"1900","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad al-Basri told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Arak ibn Malik, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He established Fifteen times in Mecca, praying two rak'ahs.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1901","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ismail ibn Muhammad informed me Bin Saad, that Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told him, that Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid told him, that he heard Al-Ala bin Al-Hadrami, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The immigrant shall remain after the end of his ritual for three days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1902","Al-Harith bin Miskin said: It was read on him, and I hear in his hadith, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Humayd, on the authority of al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Al-Hadrami, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The immigrant stayed in Mecca after that, meaning his ritual ritual for three days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1903","Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Sufi informed me. He said: Abu Nu’aym told me. He said: Al-Ala’ bin Zuhair al-Azdi told me. He said: Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad told me. On the authority of Aisha, she: She performed Umrah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Medina to Mecca, until when she came to Mecca, she said: O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. I shortened my prayers and completed them, and I broke my fast and fasted. He said: “Well done, Aisha, and he did not blame me.”"
"1904","Ahmad bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Nu`aym told me, he said: Al-Alaa bin Zuhair told us, he said: Barrah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: It was Ibn Omar: “He does not pray more than two rak’ahs during travel, and he does not pray before or after them.” So it was said to him: What is this? He said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, making"
"1905","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Issa bin Hafs bin Asim told us, he said: my father told me, he said: I was with Ibn Omar was on a journey, so he prayed the noon and afternoon prayers, two rak’ahs, then he went to his place of prayer and saw a people praising God. He said: What are these people doing? I said: They praise God. He said: If I had been praying before or after it, I would have completed it, accompanying the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was no more than On the two rak'ahs, and Abu Bakr until he was arrested, and Omar, and Othman likewise.\""
"1906","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim. He said: I am Waki’. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Tha’labah Ibn Zuhdam Al-Hanathili, he said: We were with Saeed Ibn Al-Aas from Tabaristan, and with us was Hudhayfah Ibn Al-Yaman, and he said: Which of you prayed with the Messenger of God? May God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear? Then Hudhayfah said: I am, so he described, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear with one rak’ah. He lined up behind him, and a group of Another rak'ah between him and the enemy, so he prayed one rak'ah with the group next to him, then these people retreated to the ranks of those, and those people came and prayed with them. \"a rak'ah\""
"1907","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ash’ath bin Sulaym told me, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Tha’labah ibn Zuhdam said: We were with Sa’eed ibn al-Aas in Tabaristan, and he said: Which of you prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a prayer Fear? Hudhayfah said: I am. Hudhayfah got up and arranged the people in two rows behind him. He lined up behind him, lined up parallel to the enemy, so he led a rak'ah of prayer with those behind him, and those people left to their place, and those people came and led them in prayer. rak’ah and they did not make it up.” Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Rakin bin Al-Rabi’ told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, like the prayer of Hudhayfah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1908","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He imposed “By God, prayer is on the tongue of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. It is four rak’ahs in the city, two rak’ahs when traveling, and one rak’ah in fear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1909","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Jahm told me, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led in prayer with Dhu Qard, so the people lined up behind him in two rows: one row behind him.” He lined up parallel to the enemy, and he led a rak'ah of prayer with those behind him, then they departed to their place, and those people came, and he prayed a rak'ah with them. And they did not make up for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1910","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose, and the people rose with him, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and “Allahu Akbar,” then he bowed. Some of them kneeled, then prostrated, and they prostrated, then he stood up for the second rak’ah, so those who prostrated with him fell back and guarded their brothers. And the other group came, and they knelt down with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and prostrated, and all of the people were in prayer, saying “Allahu Akbar,” but some of them kept watch. \"some\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1911","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us: My uncle told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, said: “The prayer of fear was nothing but the prayer of these guards of yours today behind These are your imams, but it was afterward, a group of them stood up, and they were all with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and prostrated. A group of people were with him, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and those who had been standing prostrated for themselves, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up. He said the salutation, and they all stood with him, then he bowed, and they all bowed with him, then he prostrated, and those who had been standing the first time prostrated with him, so when the Messenger of God sat God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and those who prostrated with him at the end of their prayer. Those who had been standing prostrated for themselves, then they sat down, and the Messenger of God gathered them together. May God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1912","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Salih bin Khawat, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah: That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He led them with the prayer of fear; he lined up in a row behind him, in a row He prayed one rak'ah with them, then they went, and those came, and he prayed one rak'ah with them, then they got up and performed one rak'ah after another.\""
"1913","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Salih bin Khawat, on the authority of the one who prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the day of Dhu al-Riqa’, he performed the fear prayer, because a group lined up with him, and a group faced the enemy, so he led those with him in prayer one rak’ah, then He remained standing, and they completed for themselves, then they left and lined up facing the enemy, and the other group came and he prayed with them the rak’ah that remained from His prayer, then he remained seated, and they completed it for themselves, then he greeted them.”"
"1914","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yusuf, he said: Saeed told us, and he is the son of Abdul Aziz, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abdullah bin Omar was narrating that he prayed the prayer of fear with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the greatest He greeted him, and he lined up a group of us behind him, and a group approached the enemy, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bowed one rak’ah with them and prostrated twice. Then they left and approached the enemy, and the other group came, and they prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did the same, then He said the salaam, then each man from the two groups stood up and prayed one rak’ah for himself and two prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1915","Imran bin Bakkar informed me, he said: Muhammad bin al-Mubarak told me, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, and Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear. He stood up and said ‘Allahu Akbar’, and a group of us prayed behind him. A group was facing the enemy, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed with them one rak’ah and prostrated two prostrations, then they left, but did not greet them. They approached the enemy and took up their positions, and the other group came and prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he led with them. One rak'ah and two prostrations, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, and he completed two rak'ahs and four prostrations, then the two groups stood up. So each one of them prayed for himself one rak’ah and two prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1916","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, he said: It was narrated by Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “One of the two groups prayed one rak’ah, and the other group faced the enemy, then they set off and stood in a position Those, those, and those came, and he prayed another rak'ah with them, then he greeted them, and those stood up, and they performed their rak'ah, and those stood up, So they performed their rak'ah.\""
"1917","Kathir bin Ubaid told me, on the authority of Baqiya, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: “ I fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before Najd, so we fought the enemy and lined up with them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose. He led us in prayer, so a group of us stood up with him, and a group approached the enemy, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kneeled down, and those with him bowed. They prostrated two times, then they left, and they were in the place of those who had not prayed, and the group that had not prayed came, so he kneeled with them one rak’ah and prostrated two times, then The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, and each Muslim man stood up and bowed for himself one rak’ah and two prostrations.”"
"1918","Abdul-A'la bin Wasil bin Abdul-A'la informed us, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi', On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear on some of his days, and a group of people stood up with him, and another group Facing the enemy, he prayed one rak'ah with those with him, then they left, and the others came, and he prayed one rak'ah with them, then the group performed one rak'ah after another.\""
"1919","Ubayd Allah bin Fadhalah bin Ibrahim told me, he said: We are Abdullah, and he is the son of Yazid al-Muqri, and Muhammad bin Abdullah told us Ibn Yazid, he said: narrated by my father, he said: narrated by Haywa, and another mentioned, he said: narrated by Abu Al-Aswad, that he heard Urwa ibn al-Zubayr speaking, on the authority of Marwan bin Al-Hakam asked Abu Hurairah: Did you pray the prayer of fear with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Abu Hurairah said: Yes, so he said: When? He said: “In the year of the Battle of Najd, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up for the afternoon prayer, and a group of people stood up with him, and another group opposite The enemy, with their backs to the Qiblah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” and so did all of them, those with him and those facing them. The enemy, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kneeled one rak’ah, and the group following him knelt with him, then he prostrated, and the group prostrated. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and the group that was with him stood up, so they went to The enemy, so they faced them, and the group that was facing the enemy came forward and they bowed and prostrated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing as Then they got up, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kneeled another rak’ah, and they knelt with him, and he prostrated, and they prostrated with him, then she came. The group that was facing the enemy, so they knelt down and prostrated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting and those with him, then the greeting came, so he greeted. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they all greeted each other. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had two rak’ahs, and each man from the two sects had to perform two rak’ahs. \"Two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1920","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told me, he said: Saeed bin Ubaid Al-Hinai told me, he said: Abdullah bin Shaqiq told us, he said: Abu Hurairah told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was camping between Dhajan and Usfan, adjacent to The polytheists, so the polytheists said: Indeed, these people have a prayer that is more important to them than their sons and firstborn, so make up your mind, then incline against them. One mile away, then Gabriel came and ordered him to divide his companions into two halves, and he would pray with one group of them and another group facing their enemy. They had taken their caution and their weapons, so he would pray a rak'ah with them, then these people would fall behind, and those people would advance, so he would pray a rak'ah with them. “There will be one rak’ah for them with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, two rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1921","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Maqsimi told me, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Muhammad, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yazid Al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led them in the prayer of fear, so a row stood in front of him, and a row behind him, and he led those behind him in prayer.” One rak'ah and two prostrations, then these people advanced until they stood in the place of their companions, and those came and took the place of these people, and the Messenger of God led them in prayer. “May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, one rak’ah, two prostrations, then the salutation. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had two rak’ahs, and one rak’ah for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1922","Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi told us, he said: Yazid al-Faqir informed me that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the prayer was established, and the Messenger of God stood up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and a group stood up behind him, and another group faced the enemy, so he prayed one rak’ah with those behind him, and prostrated with them. They prostrated two times, then they set off and took the place of those who were facing the enemy, and that group came, and the Messenger of God led the prayer with them. He prayed one rak'ah and prostrated with them two prostrations, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted those behind him and greeted those behind him. \"those\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1923","Ali bin Al-Hassan Al-Darhami and Ismail bin Masoud told us, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, On the authority of Jabir, he said: We witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear, so we stood behind him in two rows, with the enemy between us and the Qiblah. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” so we said “Allahu Akbar,” and he bowed, and we bowed, and he raised himself, and we raised, so when he descended to prostrate, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated. May God bless him and grant him peace, and those next to him, and the second row stood until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the row next to him rose, then the row prostrated. The second was in their places, then the row that was following the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell behind, and the other row advanced, so they stood in their place, and he stood up. These people are in the position of the others, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, kneeled and we kneeled, then he rose and we rose, and when he descended to prostrate, those next to him prostrated, And the others were standing, so when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and those following him rose, the others prostrated, then he gave the salutation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1924","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted a palm tree while the enemy was between us and the qiblah. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” and they all said “Allahu Akbar.” Then he bowed, so they all bowed, then The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated, and the row next to him prostrated, while the others were standing and guarding them. When they rose, the others prostrated in the place where they had been. In it, then these people advanced to the ranks of these people, and he bowed, and they all bowed, then he rose, and they all rose, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated. And the row after him, and the others were standing and guarding them. When they prostrated and sat down, the others prostrated in their place, then he said the salaam.” Jabir said: As your princes do (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1925","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I heard a mujahid speaking, On the authority of Abu Ayyash al-Zarqi, Shu`bah said: He wrote it to me, and I read it to him, and I heard him narrating it, but I memorized it, and Ibn Bashar in his hadith: I have learned from the Book that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in line with the enemy in Usfan, and against the polytheists was Khaled ibn al-Walid. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in the noon prayer. The polytheists said: “Indeed, a prayer for them after this is more beloved to them than their wealth.” And their children. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the afternoon prayer with them. He arranged them in two rows behind him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, knelt with them. They all saluted, and when they raised their heads, the next row prostrated, and the others stood up, and when they raised their heads from prostration, the back row prostrated. Because they bowed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then the front row fell behind, and the back row advanced, so each one of them stood in a position His companion, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed with them all, and when they raised their heads from bowing, the row next to him prostrated, and he stood up. The others, and when they finished prostrating, the others prostrated, and then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1926","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abdul Samad told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Ayyash al-Zarqi, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Usfan, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the noon prayer for us and for the polytheists. On that day, Khalid ibn al-Walid, and the polytheists said: We have been caught by surprise from them, so God revealed, meaning the fear prayer, during the noon prayer. And the afternoon prayer, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the afternoon prayer with us, so we separated into two groups, one group praying with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, And a group were guarding it, so he said the takbīr to those next to him and those guarding them, then he bowed, and they bowed, and all of them, then he prostrated. Those next to him, and these and those next to him lagged behind, and the others came forward and prostrated, then he got up and bowed with them all the second time, with those next to him. And with those guarding it, then he prostrated with those, meaning next to it, then they remained behind, and stayed in the rows of their companions, and the others came forward and prostrated, Then he greeted them, and each of them performed two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs with their imam, and he prayed once in the land of Banu Sulaym.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1927","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala and Ismail bin Masoud told us, and the wording is his. They said: Our Khaled, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Tomorrow: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer two rak’ahs, then he gave the salutation, then he led the people in fear two rak’ahs, then he gave the salutation.” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed four times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1928","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Amr bin Asim told me, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs with a group of his companions, then he saluted, then he prayed two rak’ahs with another group, then \"Salam\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1929","Abu Hafs Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Salih bin Khawat, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, regarding the fear prayer, he said: “The imam stands facing the Qiblah, and a group of them stands with him. And a group in front of the enemy, with their faces to the enemy, and he bowed one rak'ah with them, and they bowed for themselves, and prostrated two prostrations in their place, And they go to the place of those people, and those people come, and he kneels with them, and prostrates with them two prostrations, so there are two more for him, and for them. One rak'ah, then they bow one rak'ah after another, and prostrate two prostrations.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1930","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Ala told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he narrated, on the authority of Jabir: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted his companions and led the prayer of fear, and a group of them prayed with him, and a group of them turned their faces towards the enemy, so he prayed two rak’ahs with them, then they stood in his place. The others came, and he prayed two rak’ahs with them, then he said the salutation.”"
"1931","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “In the prayer of fear, he prayed two rak’ahs with them, and with these two rak’ahs, so it was four rak’ahs for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and two rak’ahs for them.” Two rak'ahs (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1932","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should wish for death; “It will increase in goodness, or it will increase in evil, so perhaps he will be reproached.”"
"1933","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiyya told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, the servant of Abd Al-Rahman bin Awf said that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should wish for death, as long as he is a doer of good. If he lives, his goodness will increase, and it is good for him, or he will do evil, and perhaps he will be reproached.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is more appropriate. More correct than the one before it"
"1934","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They do not wish Someone died because of harm that befell him in this world, but to say: O God, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die if death is good for me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1935","Ali bin Hajar told me, he said: Ismail, who is the son of Aliyah, told us on the authority of Abdul Aziz, and I am Imran bin Musa, he said: he told us Abdul-Warith, who said: Abdul-Aziz told us, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Doesn’t anyone wish for death because of harm?” If he must wish for death, let him say: O God, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die if death is good for me.”"
"1936","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, who was the son of Al-Hajjaj Al-Basri, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray for death, and do not wish for it.” Whoever is praying must say: O God, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die if death is good for me.”"
"1937","Anba Muhammad bin Bashar told us: Yahya told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Qais told me, he said: “We entered upon Khabab and he was suffering from His stomach was seven, and he said: Had the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not forbidden us from praying for death, I would have prayed for it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1938","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, Abu Ammar Al-Maruzi said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin reported. Al-Mubarak, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Abba Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Make frequent mention of the one who seeks pleasures.” Muhammad said in his hadith: Death. Abu Abd told us. Al-Rahman: Muhammad bin Ibrahim is the father of Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah, and Al-Qasim bin Abi Shaybah, and they are Three brothers, Abu Bakr is trustworthy, Uthman is okay with him, and Al-Qasim is not trustworthy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1939","Anba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Amash, said: A brother told me, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When you attend to the sick person, say good things, for the angels believe in what you say. When Abu Salamah died, I said: Oh Messenger of God, how should I say? He said: Say: “O God, forgive us and him, and give me after him a good deed, so God gave me after him Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1940","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Amara bin Ghaziyah told me, he said: Yahya bin Amara told me, he said: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, and Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Yahya bin Amara, On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Teach your dead that there is no god but God.”"
"1941","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ahmad bin Ishaq told me, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Mansour bin Safiya told us, on the authority of His mother, Safiya bint Shaybah, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Instruct your dead to say there is no god but God.”"
"1942","Anba Muhammad bin Bashar said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The death of a believer comes from the sweat of his brow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1943","Anba Muhammad bin Muammar said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, who is Ibn Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, who is Abdullah, on the authority of his father, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The believer dies by the sweat of his brow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1944","Anba Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Ibn al-Haad told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin al-Qasim, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died, and he is within my taste and taste, so I do not hate hardship.” Death is never for anyone after I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1945","I am Qutayba bin Saeed. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The last look I looked at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said the salaam. He opened the curtain and the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr wanted to retreat, so he motioned to them to stay, and he threw down the carpet. And he died at the end of that day, and that was a Monday.”"
"1946","Yunus bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Hayy bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman al-Hubli. On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: He said: A man who was born there died in Medina, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over him. He greeted him and said: “I wish he had died without his birth.” They said: Why is that, O Messenger of God? He said: “If a man dies without his birth, it will be measured for him from his birth until the end of his trace in Paradise,” Abu Abd told us. The Most Gracious: Yahya bin Abdullah is not one of those who can be relied upon, and this hadith is not preserved with us, and God knows best, because the authentic one is on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever of you is able to die in Medina, then I will intercede for whoever dies there.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1947","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id Abu Qudamah told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qasamah bin Zuhayr, on the authority of Ubayy Hurairah, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a believer is present, the angels of mercy will come to him with a white silk, and they will say: Go out, content and acceptable to you, to the Spirit of God, and a fragrance, and a Lord not angry, and it will come out like the sweetest scent of musk, so much so that he may give it to you. One after another, until they bring it to the gate of heaven, and they say: How good is this wind that has come to you from the earth! Then they bring it in spirits The believers have more joy over him than any of you when someone comes to him in his absence. They ask: What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? For he was in the distress of this world, and when he said: Didn’t he come to you? They said: He was taken to his mother abyss, and when the infidel comes, it comes to him? angels of torment with anointing, and they will say: Come out, angry with you, subject to the punishment of God. Then it will come out like the odor of a carrion, until they come. With it is the door to the earth, and they say: What is this smell so bad that they bring with it the souls of the disbelievers? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1948","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Zubaid, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih bin Hani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever loves meeting God, God will love meeting Him, and whoever hates meeting God, God will hate meeting him,” Shurayh said: So I went to Aisha and said: O Mother of the Believers, I heard Abu Hurairah mentioning a hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if it is like that. We have perished. She said: What is that? So you said: “Whoever loves meeting God, God will love meeting him, and whoever hates meeting God, God will hate meeting him, and there is not one of us who does not hate it.” Death, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it, but not with the one you go to, but when the sight becomes dull and the chest feels heavy. And the skin shivered, and at that time, whoever loves meeting God, God will love meeting him, and whoever hates meeting God, God will hate meeting him.”"
"1949","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, and Qutayba told us Ibn Sa`id, he said: Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He said God: If my servant loves meeting me, I love meeting him, and if my servant hates meeting me, I hate meeting him.”"
"1950","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas speaking, on the authority of Ubadah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever loves meeting God, God will love meeting Him, and whoever hates meeting God, God will hate meeting Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1951","Abu Al-Ash'ath told us, he said: Al-Mu'tamir told us, he said: I heard my father narrating, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever loves meeting God, God will love meeting Him, and whoever hates meeting God, God will hate meeting Him.”"
"1952","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: We are Abdul-Ala, he said: Saeed is us, and Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who Whoever loves meeting God, God loves meeting Him, and whoever hates meeting God, God hates meeting him.” Amr added in his hadith, and it was said: O Messenger of God, Hating meeting God, hating death, do we all hate death? He said: “That was only at the time of his death, when he was given good tidings of God’s mercy and forgiveness. He loved meeting God, and God loved meeting him, and when he was given good tidings With the punishment of God, he hated meeting God, and God hated meeting him.”"
"1953","Anba Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh said: Ibn Wahb told us: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha: “That Abu Bakr kissed the eyes of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was dead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1954","Anba Yaqoub bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Musa bin Abi Aisha told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Aisha: “Abu Bakr kissed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was dead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1955","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, he said: Anba Abdullah, Muammar said, and Yunus, Al-Zuhri said, and Abu Salamah told me that Aisha told him: That Abu Bakr rode a horse from his residence with a saddlebag, until he dismounted and entered the mosque. He did not speak to the people until he entered upon Aisha. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went on ablution, covered in a spotless hail, and uncovered his face. Then he leaned on him, kissed him, and he wept. Then he leaned on him and kissed him. He said: “By my father, by God, God will never bring two deaths together for you. As for the death that God has decreed for you, he has died.”"
"1956","Anba Muhammad bin Mansour said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Ibn al-Munkadir saying: I heard Jabir saying: My father was brought on the day of Uhud. He was mutilated and placed in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was wrapped in a garment. I wanted to uncover him, but my people forbade me. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that it be taken up. When it was taken up, he heard the voice of her crying, and he said: “Who is this?” They said: This is the daughter of Amr. He said: “So don’t cry, or why are you crying? The angels continued to shade him with their wings until he was taken up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1957","Anba Hanad bin Al-Sirri said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A daughter was present. to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a small one, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it, brought it to his chest, then put his hand She was taken, and she was in the hands of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Umm Ayman cried, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Oh! Umm Ayman, are you crying while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is with you? She said: Why should I not cry when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is crying? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am not crying, but it is mercy.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The believer He is fine in every condition, his soul is removed from his sides, and he is praising God.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib had He mixed, and the people were steadfast in it: Sufyan al-Thawri and Shu`bah ibn al-Hajjaj."
"1958","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, who said: Abba Abdul Razzaq, who said: Abba Muammar, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that Fatima wept for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace: When he died, she said: “O my father, from his Lord, how close He brought him, O my father, to Gabriel. Help him, O my father, in Paradise.” Paradise is his refuge.”"
"1959","Anba Amr ibn Yazid told us: Bahz ibn Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir that his father, He was killed on the day of Uhud. He said: I started to uncover his face and cry, while the people were forbidding me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not forbid me. My aunt made him cry, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not make him cry. The angels continued to shade him with their wings until you lifted him up.” \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1960","Abba Utbah bin Abdullah bin Utbah Al-Marwazi said: I read to Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabir. Bin Atik, that Atik bin Al-Harith, who is Abdullah bin Abdullah’s maternal grandfather, told him, that Jabir bin Atik told him: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to return Abdullah bin Thabit, and found him defeated, so he shouted at him, but he did not answer him, so the Messenger of God returned. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “We have defeated you, O Abu Al-Rabi’.” The women woke up and cried, so Ibn Atik made them silence them, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave them, and if it is necessary, do not cry.” They said: What is obligatory, O Messenger of God? He said: “Death.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1961","His daughter said: If I had hoped that you would be a martyr, you would have killed yours. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has His reward was based on his intention, and what do you count as martyrdom? They said: Killing in the cause of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are seven types of martyrdom other than killing in the cause of God: the one who is stabbed is a martyr, the one who dies is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, and the one who destroys is a martyr. The one who suffers from pleurisy is a martyr, the one who has a burn is a martyr, and the woman who dies in the plural is a martyr.”"
"1962","Abba Yunus bin Abdul-Ala said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih said, and Yahya bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, said: When the obituary came for Zaid bin Haritha, Ja’far bin Abi Talib, and Abdullah bin Rawaha, the Messenger of God sat God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: His face was known for its sadness, and I was looking from the corner of the door, then a man came to him and said: The wives of Ja’far They were crying, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go, so he forbade them.” So he went off, then he came to him and said: I have forbidden them, but they refused. They would finish, so he said: “Go,” so he forbade them. So he left, then he came to him and said: “I have forbidden them,” but he refused to let them finish, so he said: “Go.” So put dust in their mouths.” Aisha said, so I said: God forced the nose of the farthest, but by God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave it. And peace be upon you, and you will not do anything"
"1963","Abba Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abba Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Subaih, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Sirin, saying It was mentioned by Imran bin Husayn: “The dead person is tortured by the crying of the living,” and Imran said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1964","Anba Ubaid Allah bin Saeed said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The dead person is tortured because his family weeps over him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1965","Abba Suleiman bin Saif, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih, meaning Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Salem said, I heard Abdullah bin Omar saying: Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The dead person is tortured because his family weeps over him.”"
"1966","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Hakim bin Qays, that Qais bin Asim said: “Do not mourn over me, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not mourn over him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1967","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Abba Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted the women when he pledged allegiance to them not to bend, so they said: O Messenger of God, women made us happy in the pre-Islamic era, so should we make them happy? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no happiness in Islam.”"
"1968","Abba Amr bin Ali, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Omar, On the authority of Omar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The dead person is tortured in his grave by wailing over him.”"
"1969","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Saeed bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abba Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran Ibn Al-Husayn said: “The dead person is tortured with his family mourning over him.” Then a man said to him: Did you see a man who died in Khorasan and his family mourned over him here? Was he tortured because his family mourned him? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth, and you lied.”"
"1970","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The dead person is tortured because his family weeps over him.” This was mentioned to Aisha, and she said: “And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, just passed by a grave. He said: “The occupant of this grave will be tortured, and its people will weep over him.” Then I read: “And no female bearer of faith will bear the burden of another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1971","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra that she told him, that she Aisha heard, and it was reported to her, that Abdullah bin Omar said: “The dead are tortured by the crying of the living,” so Aisha said: May God forgive To Abu Abd al-Rahman. Either he did not lie, but he forgot or made a mistake. Rather, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a Jewish woman. He would cry over her, and he said: “They will cry over her, and she will be tormented.”"
"1972","Anba Abd al-Jabbar bin al-Ala bin Abd al-Jabbar, on the authority of Sufyan, said: Amr bin Dinar narrated it to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaika, He says: Ibn Abbas said, Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “God increases the punishment of the infidel with some crying.” \"His family is upon him.\""
"1973","Suleiman bin Mansour Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ward told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaika, saying: When Umm Aban died. I was present with the people, so I sat between Abdullah bin Omar and Ibn Abbas. The women cried, so Ibn Omar said: Is it not forbidden? Are these about crying? For I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The dead person is tortured because his family weeps over him.” Ibn Abbas said: Omar was Some say: I went out with Omar until we were in Al-Bayda, and he saw a group of people under a tree, so he said: Look who is in the group, so I went. So, behold, Suhaib and his family, so I returned to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, this is Suhaib and his family, and he said: Ali Suhaib, so when we entered In Medina, Omar was injured, so Suhaib sat next to him crying, and said: Oh, my brother, and my brother, so Omar said: O Suhaib, do not cry for me, for I am I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The dead person is tortured because of some of his family’s crying over him.” He said that to Aisha. She said: By God, you are not telling me this hadith, from liars or deniers, but the hearing makes mistakes, and indeed you have in the Qur’an what He will heal you. May no bearer of burden bear the burden of another. But the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God will increase the torment of the disbeliever by his weeping.” \"His family is upon him.\""
"1974","Anba Ali bin Hajar said: Ismail, he is the son of Ja’far, told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Halahla, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ataa, on the authority of Salamah ibn al-Azraq, said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: A person from the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so the women gathered together. They were crying over him, so Omar stood up and forbade them and expelled them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave them, O Omar, for the eye is watering. And the heart is afflicted, and the era is near.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1975","Ali bin Khashram reported, he said: Issa bin Yunus reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, and I am Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman bin Mujalid, he said: Ibn Idris reported. On the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of us He struck the cheeks, slit the pockets, and invoked the supplications of the people of pre-Islamic times.” Hasan said: with the supplication of the people of pre-Islamic times."
"1976","Anba Amr bin Ali told us: Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Khalid al-Ahdab, on the authority of Safwan, and he is Ibn Mahrez said: Abu Musa fainted and they cried over him, so he said: I absolve you as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, absolved us: “It is not Among us is he who has shaved, neither pierced nor shed.”"
"1977","Abba Muhammad bin Bashar, Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Zubaid told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “He is not among us who strikes the cheeks, rips the pockets, and calls upon the claims of ignorance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1978","Anba Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Awdi Al-Kufi told us: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Anba Abu Umays, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid and Abu Burdah said: When Abu Musa became heavy, his wife came crying. He said: He woke up, so he said: Pain. I tell you that I am innocent of what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was acquitted of. They said: He was telling her that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am innocent of the one who shaved, pierced, and climbed.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Abu Umays: His name is Utba bin Abdullah, and Abu Sakhrah: His name is Jami` bin Shaddad, and Abu Musa: His name is Abdullah bin Qays."
"1979","Abba Ishaq bin Mansour, he said: Abba Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “He is not among us who strikes the cheeks, rips the pockets, and calls upon the claims of ignorance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1980","Abba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Yazid bin Aws, on the authority of Abu Musa, that he fainted, and the mother of a child of his cried. When he woke up, he said to her: Have you not heard what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said? Peace be upon him, so I asked her, and she said: He said: “He who cuts, shave, and pierces is not one of us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
